      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\", mmap_mode='r')  # avoid full copy in memory upfront\n    n, d = vectors.shape\n\n    # Compute squared norms in float64 for accuracy\n    norms = np.empty(n, dtype=np.float64)\n    block_norm = 500\n    for start in range(0, n, block_norm):\n        end = min(start + block_norm, n)\n        chunk = np.asarray(vectors[start:end], dtype=np.float64)\n        norms[start:end] = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', chunk, chunk)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    B = 100  # chunk size for row blocks\n\n    # Keep a float32 copy of full vectors for matmul (already on disk, but need in-memory for dot products)\n    # Load fully once as float32 (32MB), acceptable within memory budget.\n    full = np.asarray(vectors, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for start in range(0, n, B):\n        end = min(start + B, n)\n        A = full[start:end]  # (b, d) float32\n        # dot products (b, n) in float32, then upcast for subtraction\n        dots = A @ full.T  # float32 result\n        dots = dots.astype(np.float64)\n\n        dist2 = norms[start:end][:, None] + norms[None, :] - 2.0 * dots\n        np.maximum(dist2, 0.0, out=dist2)\n        dist = np.sqrt(dist2)\n        total += dist.sum()\n\n    # Print total with fixed decimal notation, no scientific notation\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.6f}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
